      "message": "fix(sim): crossing law reads a shared vertex a rounding apart as a touch\n\nThe verifier's crossing law (a) tested orientation signs exactly, so two\nmoves meeting at one vertex reached twice, a rounding apart, could read\nas a proper crossing and hold the post. A chord end within\nCROSSING_TOUCH (1e-9 mm, a point-to-point distance) of one of the other\nchord's END points now reads as on its line, as an exact shared vertex\nalways did. Only end points are excused, not the whole line, so a walk\npassing through a chord at a vertex a picometre off its interior still\nreports (the #1134 review's probe). proper_cross itself is unchanged for\ndist2_segs and the arc-wall law.\n\nFixes #1129\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
